Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(graph):=20plugins=20on=20a=20send=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20a=20wet=20branch=20between=20the=20tap=20and=20its?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20level?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A BridgeTapSource may expose a mini-chain (getTapChain) and an envelope step
(processTapEnvelope). When the chain holds an enabled plugin the builder shares
the tapped node between the tap (dry, untouched) and a wet branch: head node
(a plain 2-channel copy), the chain's nodes, a priming gag; the tap's age is
the wet's latency. The tap lays the envelope on its copy AFTER the chain and
BEFORE the level, at the edit time the signal was made (block time minus the
copy's age): an effect's tail follows the owner's fade-out and dies at its
window's end, and a chain that adds latency keeps the envelope on the sample.
Without a chain the graph is the previous one, node for node.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
